FUN_1000_524e (engine 0x5200 driver-processing): dynamic driver-struct + ES segment base loss.

Reached from FUN_1000_5228 immediately AFTER the video driver init + mode-set complete (this is the
"0x5200 cascade" the docs root-caused as the video-DRIVER dispatch surface -- it null-derefed only because
the driver never loaded; now it does).  asm 0x1524e: bx=[DGROUP:0x736] = the driver-object struct near
offset (populated by the driver init); ax = round(param_1) clamped to <8 else 0 (an index); `xchg [bx+4]`
(old value -> return); es=[DGROUP:0x71a] (a driver template-buffer segment); si=word es:[idx]; then read
bytes es:si into struct[8] (byte), [0xa],[0xc],[0x12],[0x14] (words; p[0],p[2],p[3],p[4],p[5] -- p[1] is
skipped by an `inc si`); struct[6]=advanced si; struct[0xe]=struct[0x10]=0; then `lcall [DGROUP:0x680]`.
Ghidra dropped the DGROUP base on the struct (dereferenced the VALUE at [0x736] as a host address) and the
es=[0x71a] segment (the index/data table dereferenced as a host pointer) -> SIGSEGV, and mis-typed the word
fields as uint (4-byte).  Rebase the struct to g_mem+DGROUP+[0x736] and both lookups to the DGROUP:0x71a ES
segment with 16-bit stores.  Asm-verified base-0 0x1524e..0x152a2.
